    "summary": "Smoking Dark Star > High Time and debut Uncle John's Band, high energy",
    "blurb": "The set delivers a blazing Dark Star > High Time jam and the first-ever performance of Uncle John's Band. Black Peter shines alongside solid Good Lovin' moments, with Tom Constanten's organ adding texture throughout.",
    "review": "December 4‑’69 at the Fillmore West finds the Dead firing on all cylinders as they roll into a historic night. The band launches from Casey Jones straight into a gritty Black Peter before diving into an expansive Dark Star that segues into High Time – a jam that’s both spooky and soaring, with Jerry's Strat flirting between brilliance and a frustratingly out‑of‑tune bite. Midway through the set Pigpen’s organ swells, adding that early‑Dead texture while Tom Constanten’s rosy fills pepper the flow. The second half builds momentum into Good Lovin' and then erupts into the debut of Uncle John's Band, complete with Jerry’s tongue‑in‑cheek intro and a bass line from Phil that slugs like Jack Casady. Throughout, Mickey and Billy keep a seesaw‑style pulse that underpins the improvisations, making this show a quintessential snapshot of the band’s late‑’69 evolution.",
